---
import { getEntry, render } from "astro:content";

import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

// The second fixed page, and a page rather than a post for the structural
// reasons about.astro sets out at length: the feed's <guid isPermaLink="true">
// is a permanent subscriber-side identity, and deploy.yml accepts nothing but
// a `YYYY/MM/DD/HHmmss` slug for anything in the posts collection. Not repeated
// here -- only the part that is specific to this file is.
//
// The text itself is src/content/pages/privacy.md; this file owns the route and
// throws when the entry is missing, for the reason about.astro gives.
//
// What is specific to this page is: that text is this site's privacy policy as
// far as a reader or a regulator is concerned, and deploy.yml runs on every push
// to main whose paths touch site/**, so merging it publishes it. A placeholder therefore is
// not the harmless thing it is on the profile page -- naming an analytics
// product, a cookie or a disclosure to a third party that this site does not
// actually do would be a false statement standing on a live page. So the
// sections below name what has to be decided and assert nothing about what
// currently happens, and the first paragraph says outright that the text is
// provisional. Replace them with the real policy before pointing anyone here.
const page = await getEntry("pages", "privacy");
if (!page) throw new Error("src/content/pages/privacy.md is missing");
const { Content } = await render(page);
---

{
  /* Wrapped in <article> for the prose typography, which global.css selects from
     that element; about.astro carries the full note, including why this page is
     free to use it while the post page's <article> is not, and why no page here
     may carry a scoped <style> block. */
}
<Layout title={page.data.title} description={page.data.description}>
  <article>
    <h1>{page.data.title}</h1>
    <Content />
  </article>
  <nav class="post__back">
    <a href="/">記事一覧へ戻る</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>
